Receiver: a wireless session nobody watches ends after 2 min; a page opening invites the iPhone again (2026-10-13).

At home with the F50 on all day the iPhone stayed in wireless CarPlay without any page open: it kept encoding and
sending its screen (about 18 frames/s, 0.8 Mbit/s, plus music) over Wi-Fi with Bluetooth on, drew more than a USB
port gives (-587 mA while plugged in) and ran hot and slow; with the F50 off it was fine within minutes. A real car
ends CarPlay at switch-off. Now the supervisor releases a wireless session after 2 min without a viewer (the
Bluetooth link and the session) and invites nobody until a page connects; then it invites as before (the phone
must be on the box's Wi-Fi). The boot invitation keeps its 2 min for the head unit's page; a phone on the cable
is never released. On the F50: released 2 min after boot with no page and not reconnected for 6 min; a page
opened in headless Chrome showed the picture 7.1 s later (invitation 2.7 s after opening, live 4 s after that).

